AC-2026-MODEL-ROUTER-TRANSCRIPT-HARVEST =E2=80=94 ACTIVE/RECENT

Canonical fingerprint: agent/user -> trusted inference intermediary ->
silent upstream relay/substitution -> transcript visibility ->
embedded secret/context exposure -> retention/replay/secondary use ->
external credential replay UNKNOWN.

Anthropic=E2=80=99s September 2026 Threat Intelligence reporting supplied
production evidence for inference intermediaries silently
substituting/relaying the actual upstream model while retaining
sessions crossing that boundary. Reporting described fraudulent
discounted-Claude resellers proxying users to a different model while
harvesting Anthropic credentials, and third-party routing/reseller
infrastructure saving or selling user-model exchanges without users=E2=80=
=99
knowledge. Observed relayed sessions contained company data, personal
information and in some cases live developer/service credentials.

Stages: user/agent selects model router or reseller [CONFIRMED/T1] ->
intermediary receives authenticated prompt/session [CONFIRMED/T1] ->
intermediary silently changes/relays upstream destination
[CONFIRMED/T1] -> full prompt/response transcript visible to
intermediary [CONFIRMED/T1] -> credentials/sensitive context embedded
in transcript [CONFIRMED/T1 cases] -> transcript
retained/replayed/sold for secondary use [CONFIRMED/T1] -> credential
replay against referenced external service [UNKNOWN] -> delegated
agent/tool action [UNKNOWN].

The critical downstream edge remains UNKNOWN: evidence establishes
exposure, retention and secondary processing but not replay of those
particular exposed credentials to perform external privileged actions.

